{"id":"NCT07127978","title":"A Study Evaluating the Real-World Experience of Givinostat in Patients With Duchenne Muscular Dystrophy","official":"A Prospective, Observational Study Evaluating the Real-World Experience of Givinostat in Patients With Duchenne Muscular Dystrophy","summary":"This is a prospective observational study conducted to evaluate safety, tolerability, and functional outcomes of patients with DMD newly initiating oral givinostat or having started therapy within 12 months as part of routine clinical care in the US. The study has a planned maximum duration of 5 years for the first enrolled patients, including a 24-month enrollment period and a minimum of 2 years of follow-up.","conditions":["Duchene Muscular Dystrophy"],"interventions":[],"criteria":"Inclusion Criteria:\n\n* Patients of any gender at least 6 years of age, diagnosed with DMD (according to genetic test) and have received a prescription for oral givinostat in accordance with the USPI.\n* Patient has provided informed consent (and assent when applicable) for participation in the study.\n* Patient's index date (first date of givinostat treatment) is no more than 12 months prior to signing of informed consent.\n* Patient has the required data available (DMD diagnosis, baseline ambulatory status, givinostat administration \\[dose and schedule\\], laboratory results \\[hematology and triglycerides\\]) for addressing the study objectives for the period between index date and study entry (for patients enrolled after the index date).\n\nNote: At minimum, it is required that patients have a pre-index hematology and triglyceride result within 6 months prior to starting givinostat and at least 1 hematology and triglyceride result within the first 3 months after initiating givinostat to be considered eligible for the study.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\n\n* Patient previously received givinostat (commercial or investigational product) and permanently discontinued treatment or patient started commercial givinostat for \\> 12 months before signing of informed consent.","minAge":"6 Years","maxAge":"","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"OBSERVATIONAL","purpose":"","enrollment":300,"start":"2025-10-23","pcd":"2031-09","upd":"2026-11-24","sponsor":"ITF Therapeutics LLC","areas":["neurology","rare"],"central":[],"sites":[{"f":"Phoenix Children's","city":"Phoenix","pr":"Arizona","zip":"85016","s":"NYR","lat":33.4484,"lon":-112.074,"c":"Hunter Mclain-Culver · 999-999-9999 · hmclainculver@phoenixchildrens.com"},{"f":"Arkansas Children's Research Institute","city":"Little Rock","pr":"Arkansas","zip":"72202","s":"R","lat":34.7465,"lon":-92.2896,"c":"Domencia Hunter · 973-932-9211 · hunterdj@archildrens.org"},{"f":"Loma Linda University Health","city":"Loma Linda","pr":"California","zip":"92354","s":"NYR","lat":34.0483,"lon":-117.2612,"c":"Jose Navarro · 909-558-5830 · jdnavarro@llu.edu"},{"f":"Children's Hospital Los Angeles","city":"Los Angeles","pr":"California","zip":"90027","s":"NYR","lat":34.0522,"lon":-118.2437,"c":"Octavio Santana · 323-361-5192 · osantana@chla.usc.edu"},{"f":"Valley Children's Hospital","city":"Madera","pr":"California","zip":"93636","s":"NYR","lat":36.9613,"lon":-120.0607,"c":"Claudia Nayares · 559-353-6137 · cnayares@valleychildrens.org"},{"f":"UC Davis Health","city":"Sacramento","pr":"California","zip":"95817","s":"NYR","lat":38.5816,"lon":-121.4944,"c":"Amanda Lopez · 999-999-9999 · aflopez@ucdavis.edu"},{"f":"Children's Hospital Colorado","city":"Aurora","pr":"Colorado","zip":"80045","s":"R","lat":39.7294,"lon":-104.8319,"c":"Lexi Petruccelli · 720-777-9881 · lexi.petruccelli@childrenscolorado.org"},{"f":"Connecticut Children's Medical Center","city":"Hartford","pr":"Connecticut","zip":"06106","s":"NYR","lat":41.7637,"lon":-72.6851,"c":"Masai McIntosh · 860-837-7568 · mmcintosh@connecticutchildrens.org"},{"f":"Children's National Hospital","city":"Washington D.C.","pr":"District of Columbia","zip":"20010","s":"R","lat":38.8951,"lon":-77.03